[17592186406605 1080 #uuid "3d4d9909-2b00-5980-9b7e-95f491417da2" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406592 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406594 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406595 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406597 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406604 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406606 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406606 1077 "selection" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406606 1079 #edb/ref 17592186406592 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406606 1080 #uuid "83d8f167-e779-56fd-836e-ab6aac4f2070" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406607 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406591 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406607 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406593 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406607 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406596 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406607 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406600 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406607 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406602 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406607 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406607 1077 "selection" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406607 1079 #edb/ref 17592186406593 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406607 1080 #uuid "d1825133-7014-5a09-9154-148509062f75" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406608 1068 #edb/ref 17592186406605 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406608 1069 "q-65581" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406608 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406608 1071 "Given that the expression $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406608 1072 #uuid "139292f5-27c6-5b2f-8f13-1b15372d0a1a" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406608 1074 "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{6}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =3 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406609 1068 #edb/ref 17592186406607 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406609 1069 "q-65578" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406609 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406609 1071 "Given that the expression $\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406609 1072 #uuid "79089117-3e5a-51ff-ae41-40a7e2901f6d" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406609 1074 "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{3} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ ϕ & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406610 1068 #edb/ref 17592186406606 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406610 1069 "q-11294" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406610 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406610 1071 "$3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=$" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406610 1072 #uuid "e58d0138-9eca-5984-8b18-90ecf02f0d0d" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406610 1074 "The difference formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=3 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =1 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1) \\\\ ϕ & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={3}^{2}+(3)^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =2\\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2} & =18 \\\\ R & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{45}^{∘})\n$$" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406611 1058 #edb/ref 17592186406612 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406611 1062 #uuid "a06f20a6-d2e4-56ba-a165-46b7fcfbdf95" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406611 1063 #edb/ref 17592186406609 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406612 1062 #uuid "cc02456f-a095-5e41-95ce-6a946f125439" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406612 1063 #edb/ref 17592186406608 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406613 1058 #edb/ref 17592186406611 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406613 1062 #uuid "fe07e852-ca7d-55ad-9fb8-dab24d09b6c8" 13194139533510 17592186045585 true] [17592186406613 1063 #edb/ref 17592186406610 131941